{{!
    @template aiplacement_dimensions/pickers

    Framework select plus the branch checkboxes that scope the request.

    branchesshown, branchestotal and branchestruncated describe the root competencies
    page fetched for the framework currently on screen: the server paginates at 25,
    so branchestruncated is true whenever branchestotal is larger than branches.length,
    and the fieldset then carries a notice instead of silently dropping the rest.

    The wrapper below is a div, not a form, on purpose. This markup is only ever injected
    via body.innerHTML into aiplacement_dimensions/drawer's body, which itself lives inside
    the activity edit page's own <form> (see lib.php: the drawer is a MoodleQuickForm static
    element placed right before the "competencies" field). A <form> nested inside a live
    <form> ancestor is invalid HTML, and per the HTML parsing spec a browser parsing such
    markup through innerHTML silently drops the inner <form> start tag while still inserting
    its children -- so the wrapping element, and any class or selector on it, would never
    actually exist in the DOM. This was reproduced directly against Chrome (not inferred from
    the spec alone): setting innerHTML with a <form> wrapper on a div already nested inside a
    live <form> element yields child content but no <form> node, while the identical markup
    parses correctly on a detached node. Nothing here reads this element as a real form
    (suggest.js reads the select's value and the checkboxes' checked state directly, and
    never uses FormData or a submit handler), so a div loses no behaviour.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "frameworks": [{"id": 1, "shortname": "Framework"}],
        "branches": [{"id": 9, "shortname": "Root"}],
        "branchesshown": 1,
        "branchestotal": 1,
        "branchestruncated": false
    }
}}
<div class="aiplacement-dimensions-pickers">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <label class="form-label" for="aiplacement-dimensions-framework">
            {{#str}} frameworklabel, aiplacement_dimensions {{/str}}
        </label>
        <select class="form-select" id="aiplacement-dimensions-framework" data-region="framework">
            {{#frameworks}}<option value="{{id}}">{{shortname}}</option>{{/frameworks}}
        </select>
    </div>

    {{#branches.length}}
        <fieldset class="mb-3">
            <legend class="h6">{{#str}} brancheslabel, aiplacement_dimensions {{/str}}</legend>
            {{#branchestruncated}}
                <p class="aiplacement-dimensions-branches-notice small text-muted">
                    {{#str}} branchestruncated, aiplacement_dimensions,
                        {"shown": {{#quote}}{{branchesshown}}{{/quote}}, "total": {{#quote}}{{branchestotal}}{{/quote}}}
                    {{/str}}
                </p>
            {{/branchestruncated}}
            {{#branches}}
                <div class="form-check">
                    <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" value="{{id}}"
                           id="aiplacement-dimensions-branch-{{id}}" data-region="branch">
                    <label class="form-check-label" for="aiplacement-dimensions-branch-{{id}}">{{shortname}}</label>
                </div>
            {{/branches}}
        </fieldset>
    {{/branches.length}}

    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="aiplacement-dimensions-run">
        {{#str}} runbutton, aiplacement_dimensions {{/str}}
    </button>
</div>
